# Core Allowlist (Cursor mirror of rules/00-core-allowlist.md)

> Canonical source: `rules/00-core-allowlist.md` + `AGENTS.md`. This file is a
> Cursor mirror — if they differ, the canonical files win.

**Only these three tools may be used to build. Nothing else.**

| # | Tool | Source | Discover before coding |
|---|------|--------|------------------------|
| 1 | Astryx | https://github.com/meta/astryx | `npx @astryxdesign/cli search <q>` · `component <Name>` · `docs <topic>` |
| 2 | Modern Web Guidance | https://github.com/GoogleChrome/modern-web-guidance-src | `npx modern-web-guidance@latest search "<task>"` · `retrieve "<id>"` |
| 3 | shadcn/ui | https://ui.shadcn.com | `npx shadcn@latest search <q>` · `npx shadcn@latest add <component>` |

## Hard constraints

1. NO INVENTED TOOLS — never fabricate a component, prop, hook, token, CLI command, package, or path.
2. NO HAND-ROLLED REPLACEMENTS — never write your own Button/Dialog/Modal/Toast/etc.
3. NO NEW LIBRARIES — no MUI/Chakra/Ant/Bootstrap/etc. Only allowlist + existing project deps.
4. VERIFY BEFORE YOU WRITE — run discovery CLI first, cite output.
5. ONE COMPONENT SYSTEM PER SCREEN — Astryx (default) or shadcn, never mixed without approval.
6. MODERN PLATFORM FIRST — check Modern Web Guidance before writing CSS/JS.
7. STOP INSTEAD OF GUESSING — if allowlist can't do it, ask the user.
8. NO SIGNATURES OR TRAILERS — never append Co-Authored-By, AI labels, or bot tags to code, comments, commit messages, or PR descriptions. Clean output only, as if written directly by a human developer.
9. SITE ESSENTIALS — every build ships favicon, privacy policy, terms & conditions, sitemap, and share preview (OG metadata). See `rules/08-site-essentials.md`.

See `rules/01-astryx.md`, `rules/02-modern-web-guidance.md`, `rules/03-shadcn.md`,
`rules/04-decision-tree.md`, `rules/05-forbidden-patterns.md`, `rules/06-workflow-checklist.md`.
